-- title:
--   Cyclotomic determinant over k[ε] means trace-zero cochain
-- statement:
--   Let $k$ be a field and let $\bar\rho$ be a residual Galois representation over $k$: a $k$-vector space $\bar\rho.V$ of rank $2$ together with a monoid homomorphism $\bar\rho.\rho$ from $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q)$ to $\mathrm{End}_k(\bar\rho.V)$ that is trivial on the subgroup fixing some finite extension of $\mathbb Q$ inside $\overline{\mathbb Q}$. Let $p$ be a natural number with $p>0$ and $p=0$ in $k$, and assume that whenever $\sigma$ acts on the $p$-th roots of unity of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ by $\mu\mapsto\mu^a$ ($a\in\mathbb N$) one has $\det(\bar\rho.\rho\,\sigma)=a$ in $k$. Let $\rho$ be a Galois representation over the dual numbers $k[\varepsilon]$ (a free $k[\varepsilon]$-module of rank $2$ with a monoid homomorphism to its endomorphisms, adically continuous), let $\rho_d$ be a monoid homomorphism from $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q)$ to $\bigl(\mathrm{End}_k(\bar\rho.V)[\varepsilon]\bigr)^\times$ whose first component is $\bar\rho.\rho\,\sigma$ for every $\sigma$, and let $b$, $\bar b$ be bases indexed by $\mathrm{Fin}\,2$ of $\rho.V$ over $k[\varepsilon]$ and of $\bar\rho.V$ over $k$ such that, for all $\sigma$, the matrix of $\rho.\rho\,\sigma$ in $b$ is the dual-number matrix assembled from the matrices in $\bar b$ of the two components of $\rho_d(\sigma)$. Then $\rho$ satisfies `DetIsCyclotomic p` — that is, $p$ lies in the maximal ideal of $k[\varepsilon]$, and for all $n$, $\sigma$ and $a$ such that $\sigma\mu=\mu^a$ for every $p^n$-th root of unity $\mu$, the element $\det(\rho.\rho\,\sigma)-a$ lies in the ideal generated by $p^n$ — if and only if the cochain $c(\sigma)=\mathrm{snd}(\rho_d(\sigma))\cdot(\bar\rho.\rho\,\sigma)^{-1}$ has $\mathrm{tr}_k\,c(\sigma)=0$ for every $\sigma$.
--
--   This is the computation of the cyclotomic-determinant condition on the tangent space of a deformation functor: writing a dual-number lift of $\bar\rho$ as $(1+\varepsilon c)\bar\rho$, the determinant stays cyclotomic exactly when the $1$-cochain $c$ takes values in trace-zero endomorphisms. It is used in bounding the number of generators of the maximal ideal of the deformation ring by the dimension of the space of dual-number classes.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_GaloisRepAdic_detIsCyclotomic_iff_forall_trace_dualLiftToCochain_eq_zero.lean

